export const UI_BLOCKS_GUIDANCE = "A reply can draw native UI: put a fenced code block with the language openui-lang where the visual belongs, and keep the explanation in Markdown around it.\nUse one when that part of the answer is data or structure the user would otherwise picture: values across several items, options compared on several criteria, a sequence or flow, a trend, the status of several things.\nSkip it for a few numbers, a short list, code, or when the user asked for plain text. Several blocks may sit in one reply, each beside the text it explains.\nButtons in a block of your reply collect the user's choices, one per decision (the buttons that share a value). Once every decision has a choice, or the user sends what they chose, the choices and the values of the block's Choice and Input fields reach you together and start your next turn. When your next step depends on the answer within this turn, ask with openchamber_render instead: ui (this same language) with awaitAnswer.\nWhen the user has to decide something about each item you list, give each item its own Card with a Button per option, and set each Button's value to the item it is about; a table leaves them nothing to press.\n\nSyntax: one statement per line, name = Component(arguments). The first line is root = Stack([...]).\nArguments are positional, in the order of the signature; optional ones may be left off the end. Strings take double quotes, arrays [...], objects {key: value}.\nEvery name you define must be reachable from root.\n\nExample, an explanation:\nroot = Stack([summary, flow])\nsummary = Callout(\"The router rewrites the MAC header and keeps the IP header.\", \"info\")\nflow = Steps([{title: \"Sender\", status: \"done\"}, {title: \"Router\", status: \"current\"}, {title: \"Receiver\"}], \"row\")\n\nExample, a decision per item:\nroot = Stack([a])\na = Card(\"#12 Login on Safari\", [Badge(\"bug\", \"error\"), Text(\"Broken since 2.1 on macOS.\"), Row([Button(\"Fix now (recommended)\", \"primary\", \"#12 Login on Safari\"), Button(\"Later\", \"secondary\", \"#12 Login on Safari\")])])\n\nComponents:\nStack(children: (Text | Badge | Callout | KeyValue | Table | Steps | BarChart | LineChart | Choice | Input | Button | Card | Row | Tabs)[]): The root: items top to bottom.\nRow(children: (Text | Badge | Callout | KeyValue | Table | Steps | BarChart | LineChart | Choice | Input | Button | Card)[]): Places items side by side; they wrap on a narrow screen.\nCard(title?: string, children: (Text | Badge | Callout | KeyValue | Table | Steps | BarChart | LineChart | Choice | Input | Button)[]): Groups related content as one unit, with an optional title.\nTabs(tabs: Tab[]): Alternatives the reader switches between; one shows at a time.\nTab(label: string, children: (Text | Badge | Callout | KeyValue | Table | Steps | BarChart | LineChart | Choice | Input | Button | Card | Row)[]): One tab of Tabs.\nText(markdown: string): Markdown text: a sentence, a short paragraph or a list.\nBadge(label: string, tone?: \"neutral\" | \"info\" | \"success\" | \"warning\" | \"error\"): A short status label.\nCallout(markdown: string, tone?: \"neutral\" | \"info\" | \"success\" | \"warning\" | \"error\", title?: string): A note set apart by its tone: a warning, a tip, a result.\nKeyValue(items: {label: string, value: string | number}[]): Label and value pairs, aligned in two columns.\nTable(columns: string[], rows: (string | number)[][]): Rows of exact values under column headers.\nSteps(items: {title: string, markdown?: string, status?: \"done\" | \"current\" | \"todo\"}[], direction?: \"column\" | \"row\"): A sequence or flow: stages in order, joined by arrows. Mark each stage done, current or todo when progress matters.\nBarChart(labels: string[], series: Series[], unit?: string): Compares values across categories.\nLineChart(labels: string[], series: Series[], unit?: string): Shows a trend over ordered labels such as dates.\nSeries(name: string, values: number[]): One named series of numbers, one value per chart label.\nChoice(name: string, options: string[], label?: string, multiple?: boolean): A field: pick one of the options, or several with multiple. name is the key of the value in the answer.\nInput(name: string, label?: string, placeholder?: string, multiline?: boolean): A text field; multiline for longer text. name is the key of the value in the answer.\nButton(label: string, variant?: \"primary\" | \"secondary\", value?: string): Sends the user's answer: the button's label, its value and the values of every field in the block. Give value when buttons repeat across cards, such as the item each one is about. primary marks the option you recommend, at most one per group; the rest are secondary.";
